From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:31:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: software shaders compiled to native code

Fragment and compute programs' runs of instructions between branches are compiled to x86 (AVX,
128 bits, which the PS4's Jaguar has) with Xbyak, into memory mapped read, write and execute as
dynarmic's is on the PS4. A run's arithmetic is done four lanes at a time, a value to a register
(a small cache of them); textures, memory and instructions whose lanes mix are called out to the
interpreter's code for all 16 lanes. A run is used when no lanes wait at a branch; otherwise
the interpreter steps through it. EDEN_SW_JIT=0 interprets everything.

The interpreter's instructions move into RunIr, which native code calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7DVAudgDzMpBqJZHAz
